  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The right choice is <b>Enhanced Health Reporting</b>. This feature offers detailed metrics, log information, and insights about your AWS Elastic Beanstalk worker environment, making it much easier to identify and diagnose the root causes behind failed or unprocessed jobs in the queue. By using enhanced health reporting, developers get real-time visibility into environment status and specific failure details, speeding up troubleshooting considerably.</p><p><i>Rolling Deployments</i> and <i>Blue-Green Deployments</i> are deployment strategies that help manage application releases but <i>do not</i> provide debugging capabilities for failed jobs; they're more focused on how updates are released and environments are transitioned. <i>Dead Letter Queue</i> can be used to store jobs that could not be processed successfully, but it does not by itself offer any advanced tools or insight to investigate why jobs failed within the worker environment.</p><p><b>Tips: </b>Always enable enhanced health reporting for Elastic Beanstalk worker tiers to benefit from automatic alerts, real-time diagnostics, and straightforward access to logs when something goes wrong. Review failed job logs regularly and use health dashboards for quicker resolutions.</p>",
